# =============================================================================
# SmartCycle .gitignore
# =============================================================================

# --- Python virtual environments ---------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/

# --- Python caches and generated files ---------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- Node dependencies and build output --------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.vite/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# --- Local environment files --------------------------------------------------
# Real configuration and secrets. Only the *.example templates are committed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Local SQLite databases ---------------------------------------------------
# DELIBERATE DECISION: the database is NOT committed.
#
# This is not a blanket "ignore all databases" rule. It is a considered choice,
# because backend/smartcycle.db contains real records: user accounts with
# Argon2 password hashes, device submissions with owner names, email addresses,
# street addresses and locations, and pickup requests with collection
# addresses. Committing it would publish personal data and a credential
# database to anyone who clones the repository, and it would grow on every run.
#
# The application does not need it: `init_db()` creates the schema on first
# start, and a fresh clone gets an empty, fully working system. To reproduce the
# demo data, register a user, submit devices, and create an admin with
#   python -m app.scripts.create_admin
#
# If a seeded database were ever wanted for a demo, the correct approach is a
# separate, deliberately sanitised fixture (no real emails, addresses or
# password hashes) plus a documented seeding script - not this working file.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# --- Trained ML artifacts -----------------------------------------------------
# backend/data/valuation_model.joblib is a ~3.9 MB binary derived entirely from
# the committed synthetic dataset, so it is fully regenerable with:
#   python -m app.scripts.train_valuation_model
#
# It is deliberately not committed: it is a build output, not source. The API
# does not require it - when the file is absent the rule-based estimator is
# used automatically and each result is labelled "rule_based".
#
# The dataset and the metrics sidecar ARE committed, because they are small,
# human-readable and needed to understand and reproduce the training.
backend/data/*.joblib
backend/data/*.pkl
backend/data/*.h5

# --- Logs and temporary files -------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/
tmp/
temp/
.cache/
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig
*.swp
*~

# --- Local agent / tooling artifacts ------------------------------------------
# Session transcripts and scratch files produced by development tools. They can
# contain internal identifiers and raw conversation content, so they must never
# enter the repository.
*-project-plan.json
*.session.json
.agent/
.codex/

# --- Editor and operating-system files ----------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
*.sublime-workspace
*.sublime-project
